course: dictionary
lesson: 9906
title: Tall: height and meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tall means high from the bottom to the top. A giraffe is tall because it reaches high up. In «tall towers are struck many times a year», tall tells you how high each tower stands.
explain: Tall helps us compare heights. «Kieran competes with Sam at everything: who's taller, who runs faster» uses taller to compare two boys. Taller is the comparing form, and tallest is for the highest of all.
explain: Tall can also mean hard to believe, as in a tall story. Tall is also in phrases like «stand tall», which means to be proud and brave. Look at the words around tall to choose the right meaning.
fact: Tall means high from the bottom to the top.
fact: The forms are tall, taller and tallest: use taller for two things and tallest for three or more.
fact: «Lincoln Cathedral in England was probably the tallest building in the world for about 200 years, until its spire fell in 1548.»
fact: A tall story, or tall tale, is one that is hard to believe.
fact: You can say how tall someone is with a measure, as in «he is 150 cm tall».
exercise: «Lightning can strike the same place more than once; tall towers are struck many times a year.» What does tall mean here? | Very thin and bendy | Very loud | *High from the bottom to the top | Full of water
exercise: Kieran says, «I am taller than Sam.» Which word compares two boys by height? | talling | tallest | tall | *taller
exercise: «He is 150 cm tall.» What does tall tell us about him? | *How high he is, from his feet to his head | How old he is | How much he weighs | How fast he can run
test: Ben tells a tall tale about flying to the moon. What is a tall tale? | A short poem | *A story that is hard to believe | A story about a very high tower | A true story about the sea
test: Which phrase means to be proud and brave? | run fast | sit still | *stand tall | fall down
exam: Tom says, «Lincoln Cathedral was the tallest building.» What does tallest mean? | *Higher than all the others | Most colourful | Newest of all | Shortest of all
